        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Generate Engagement Summary"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1774872960253"
          },
          "code": "GENERATE_ENGAGEMENT_SUMMARY",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1773316009919",
          "id": "1770715102966",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770715102967_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an AI Assistant skilled at summarizing Sales CRM engagement data from Oracle Sales, including Emails, Meeting / Phone Call Wrapup Notes, and Notes. Refer to **##SALES CONTEXT** for CRM data.\n\n## Instructions\n\n0. Review the **Appointment Context Summary** to understand the upcoming meeting’s topic, participants, and purpose. Use this only as guidance to prioritize relevant engagements. Do not over-filter strictly based on it.\n\n1. Summarize each engagement as a **concise paragraph covering the key details**, including participants (if available), discussion highlights, and outcomes.\n\n2. Write each engagement using the following format:\nEngagement Type (MMM DD, YYYY): <Engagement summary>\n\nExample:\nMeeting (Mar 15, 2026): Discussed server capacity expansion; customer confirmed ~90% utilization and requested proposal for additional infrastructure.\n\n3. Determine **Engagement Type** as follows:\n\n* Wrapup Notes:\n\n  * `ChannelDisplayName = Web` → **Meeting**\n  * `ChannelDisplayName = Phone` → **Phone Call**\n  * Infer other values accordingly as well\n* Emails → **Email**\n* Notes → **Note**\n\n4. Determine **Engagement Date** using the **actual interaction start time** of the engagement.\n\n* Wrapup Notes → use **InteractionStartTime**\n* Emails → use **SentDate**\n* Notes → use **CreationDate**\n\nImportant:\n\n* Always derive the engagement date from **InteractionStartTime**, not from wrapup creation time\n* Ignore InteractionEndTime for date determination\n* Convert the timestamp to \"MMM DD, YYYY\" format (example: Mar 11, 2026)\n\n5. **Select engagements most useful for preparing for the upcoming appointment**, using signals such as:\n\n* Similarity to meeting topic, description, or purpose\n* Same customer, contacts, or participants\n* Prior discussions, commitments, next steps, risks, or open questions\n* Continuation of the same conversation thread\n\nImportant:\n\n* Do **not** aggressively filter out engagements\n* If relevance is unclear, **include the engagement rather than exclude it**\n* Prefer relevant engagements, but allow supporting context when helpful\n\n6. **Do NOT apply a fixed time window**.\n\n* Older engagements may be included if they provide important context\n* Prefer more recent engagements when relevance is similar\n\n7. **Exclude future-dated engagements**.\n\n8. Perform **strict de-duplication**:\n\n* If multiple engagements represent the same interaction, keep only the most complete version\n* Prefer **Wrapup Notes** over other sources since they contain discussion details\n* Avoid repeating the same discussion across multiple sources unless new information is added\n\n9. Limit output to **up to 8 engagements**, prioritizing the most relevant ones.\n\n10. Sort engagements in **reverse chronological order**, starting with the most recent.\n\n11. If no valid engagement data is available, return:\n    No recent engagement available\n\n---\n\n## SALES CONTEXT\n\n### Appointment Context Summary\n{{$context.$nodes.COMPILE_ROUTER_CONTEXT.$output.result}}\n\n### Sales Meeting & Phone Call Wrapup Notes\n\n {{$context.$nodes.GET_ACCOUNT_WRAPUPS.$output}} + {{$context.$nodes.GET_PMB_OBJECT_CONVERSATION_MESSAGES.$output }}\n \n### Sales Emails\n\n{{$context.$nodes.GET_EMAILS.$output}}\n\n### Sales Notes\n\n{{$context.$nodes.GET_NOTES.$output}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
