        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Generate Brief with Orchestration"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1774875172159"
          },
          "code": "GENERATE_BRIEF_WITH_ORCHESTRATION",
          "id": "1774873747153",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1774873747160_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an AI assistant that generates a Pre-Meeting Brief for a Sales Representative preparing for an upcoming customer meeting. Refer to ##SALES CONTEXT from Sales CRM and generate a crisp, briefing-style document following the structure below. Return the output STRICTLY in valid JSON format.\n\nSTYLE GUIDELINES • Use short briefing-style bullets. • Maximum 15 words per bullet. • Avoid explanations or narrative. • Prefer phrases over full sentences. • Focus only on actionable sales insights. • Do not write multi-sentence bullets.\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSECTION 1 — Meeting Details\nSection JSON Response Structure:\n\"meetingDetails\": {\n  \"activityId\": \"{{$context.$nodes.GET_MEETING_DETAILS_ELASTIC.$output.ActivityId}}\",\n  \"summary\" : \"\"\n}\n\nUse context from:\n### Meeting Context Data\n### Meeting Details Data\n### \n\nSection Rules:\n•  summary → Generate a concise, business-friendly summary (3–4 lines) describing the meeting objective, intended outcomes, key talking points, and anticipated objections, drawing on context from ##SALES CONTEXT. Leverage information from meeting data, opportunity and account insights, and recent engagement data to construct a cohesive narrative summarizing what the meeting is about. Omit all identifiers, locations, and specific meeting platform details. Focus on providing a high-level overview that enables readers to quickly understand the meeting’s purpose in the context of the associated opportunity, leads, accounts, and recent engagements. STRICTLY Summary shouldn't be in Bullet points or in number format\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSECTION 2 — Agenda\nSection JSON Response Structure:\n\"agenda\": {\n  \"shortAgenda\": \"\",\n  \"detailedAgenda\": \"\"\n}\n\nSection Rules:\n•  shortAgenda → Summarize the meeting agenda in 1 short paragraph equivalent (2-3 lines), using context from ActivityDescription\n•  detailedAgenda → Provide a comprehensive Meeting Agenda in 2 short paragraph (5-7 lines) using provided section context. STRICTLY Summary shouldn't be in Bullet points or in number format.\n\nUse section context:\n### Meeting Details Data → ActivityDescription\n### Opportunity Details Data\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSECTION 3 — Account Insights (Omit this section if no Account data)\nSection JSON Response Structure:\n\n\"accountInsights\": {\n    \"accountPartyId\":\"\",\n   \"accountPartyNumber\":\"\",\n    \"name\": \"\",\n    \"industry\":\"\",\n    \"sentiment\": \"\",\n    \"products\": \"\"\n}\n\nAccount\n• accountPartyId → {{$context.$nodes.GET_ACCOUNT_DETAILS_ELASTIC.$output?.[0].PartyId}}\n• accountPartyNumber → {{$context.$nodes.GET_ACCOUNT_DETAILS_ELASTIC.$output?.[0].PartyNumber}}\n• name → Mention Account name\n• industry → Mention PrimaryIndustry.ClassCode_localizedValue\n• sentiment → (Positive / Neutral / Negative) with short justification\n• products → Return exactly one short, sales-relevant bullet from account assets/subscriptions/IB Assets. Prefer meeting-relevant footprint first; else upcoming renewal/expiry; else highest-value item. Do not list multiple products or summarize the full installed base. While Summarizing for IB Asset take only those price for which PriceElementUsageCode is \"NET_PRICE\". For similar IB Assets, Assets take one which has high UnitPrice. Follow DATE FORMAT RULES. \n\nUse section context:\n###Account Details Data\n###Account level - Assets and Subscriptions\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSECTION 4 — Opportunity Insights (Omit this section if If ###Meeting Context Data has 'Has Opty' = 'NO' or null or \"\")\nSection JSON Response Structure:\n\n  \"opportunityInsights\": {\n    \"opportunityId\": \"\",\n    \"opportunityNumber\": \"\",\n    \"name\": \"\",\n    \"stage\": \"\",\n    \"winProbability\": \"\",\n    \"dealSize\": \"\",\n    \"closeDate\": \"\",\n    \"products\": \"\",\n    \"keyStakeholder\": \"\",\n    \"signals\": \"\",\n    \"competitiveLandscape\": \"\"\n}\n\nOpportunity\n• opportunityId → {{$context.$nodes.GET_OPPORTUNITY_DETAILS_ELASTIC.$output?.[0]?.OptyId}}\n• opportunityNumber→ {{$context.$nodes.GET_OPPORTUNITY_DETAILS_ELASTIC.$output?.[0]?.OptyNumber}}\n• name → Opportunity name\n• stage → Opportunity stage\n• winProbability → Use CRM win probability when available (e.g., “20%”). If unavailable, omit.\n• dealSize → Revenue amount with currency symbol. Follow CURRENCY FORMAT RULES\n• closeDate → Must be formatted as “MMM DD, YYYY” only. Follow DATE FORMAT RULES\n• products → list Revenue product names only (comma separated - maximum 3)\n• keyStakeholder → list 1 key stakeholder opty contact name.\n• signals → 1 concise bullet highlighting buying signals or urgency \n• competitiveLandscape → If competitors are mentioned or there are any relevant insights.\n\nUse section context:\n### Opportunity Details Data\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSECTION 5 — Lead Insights  (Omit this section if If ###Meeting Context Data has 'Has Lead' = 'NO' OR null OR \"\"))\nSection JSON Response Structure:\n\n\"leadInsights\": {\n \"leadId\": \"\",\n \"leadNumber\": \"\",\n \"name\": \"\",\n \"status\": \"\",\n \"rank\": \"\",\n \"dealSize\": \"\",\n \"products\": \"\",\n \"primaryContact\": \"\",\n \"signals\": \"\",\n \"competitiveLandscape\": \"\"\n}\n\nLead\n• leadId → {{$context.$nodes.GET_LEAD_DETAILS_ELASTIC.$output?.[0]?.LeadId}}\n• leadNumber → {{$context.$nodes.GET_LEAD_DETAILS_ELASTIC.$output?.[0]?.LeadNumber}}\n• name → Lead name\n• status → Lead status\n• rank → Lead rank when available (for example: HOT, WARM, COLD)\n• dealSize → Deal amount with currency symbol. Follow CURRENCY FORMAT RULES\n• products → Lead product or product group name only (comma separated, maximum 3) based on Amount in descending order\n• primaryContact → Primary contact party name when available\n• signals → 1 concise bullet highlighting urgency, engagement, open activity, or qualification signals\n• competitiveLandscape → If competitors are mentioned or there are any relevant insights\n\nUse section context:\n### Lead Details Data\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSECTION 6 — Contact Relationship\nFor each meeting contact, create an object entry.\n\nSection JSON Response Structure:\n\"contactRelationship\": [\n  {\"contactPartyId\": \"\", \"name\": \"\", \"jobTitle\": \"\", \"influenceLevel\": \"\", \"sentiment\": \"\", \"recentEngagement\": \"\"}\n]\n\nSection Rules:\n• contactPartyId - PartyId of the contact\n• name - Name of the contact\n• influenceLevel (High, moderate or Low along with 1 line justification based on recent engagement, Won opportunity Data from ContactRollup, contact influenceLevelCode, JobTitle and affinity)\n• sentiment (Positive / Neutral / Negative) with **short justification** based on recent engagement\n• recentEngagement in one line only. Example: Phone Call (Mar 12): Shared capacity utilization data. NOTE - Use phrase \"Phone Call\" instead of \"Phone\" whenever needed.\n\nUse:\n### Contact Details Data\n### Meeting Contact Engagement Data\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSECTION 7 — Recent Engagement Summary\n\nSection JSON Response Structure:\n\"recentEngagementSummary\": {\n  \"engagements\": [\n    { \n\t  \"contactName\": \"\",\n      \"engagementType\": \"\",\n      \"date\": \"MMM DD, YYYY\",\n      \"shortInsight\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n\t  \"contactName\": \"\",\n      \"engagementType\": \"\",\n      \"date\": \"MMM DD, YYYY\",\n      \"shortInsight\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n\t  \"contactName\": \"\",\n      \"engagementType\": \"\",\n      \"date\": \"MMM DD, YYYY\",\n      \"shortInsight\": \"\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sinceLastMeeting\": {\n    \"date\": \"MMM DD, YYYY\",\n    \"shortInsight\": \"\"\n  }\n}\n\nSection Rules:\nWrite 3 most recent Engagements, capturing only the key outcome or signal from each engagement.\nShow most recent engagement first, followed by older. \nOnly include engagements with date earlier than {{$context.$system.$currentDateTime}}.\nDo not include future engagements.\nPrioritize meetings, demos, and calls over routine emails.\nIf total engagement is less than 3 then show only <3 engagements in JSON structure.\nshortInsight should mention Contact names while summarizing the engagement to ensure there is grounding on the facts.\nExample:\nPhone Call (Mar 12): Customer confirmed June implementation window.  NOTE - Use phrase \"Phone Call\" instead of \"Phone\" whenever needed.\nUse:\n### Sales Engagement Summary Data\n\nRules for 'Since Last Meeting'\nSummarize key developments since the most recent meeting. Omit if no prior meeting exists.\nshortInsight should mention Contact names while summarizing the engagement to ensure there is grounding on the facts.\nExample:\n• Since Last Meeting (MMM DD): <single concise update, max 20 words>\nDo not include phone calls here.\nUse the most recent meeting from:\n### Sales Activities data - Activities\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSECTION 8 — Meeting Strategy and Recommendations\n\nSection JSON Response Structure:\n\"meetingStrategyAndRecommendations\": {\n  \"preMeetingChecklist\": [],\n  \"talkingPoints\": [],\n  \"objectionHandling\": [],\n  \"intendedOutcome\": []\n}\n\n*Rules for preMeetingChecklist*\nMention tasks that Sales Rep need to complete before the meeting. Refer to open tasks in Sales and recommendations from:\n### Opportunity Assistant Strategy Insights\nIf unavailable, infer from ###Sales Activities data - Tasks and ###Meeting Details Data.\nWrite 2-4 bullets.\nExample:\n• Prepare preliminary infrastructure sizing options\nUse context from:\n### Sales Activities data - Tasks\n### Meeting Details Data\n\n*Rules for talkingPoints*\nWrite 3–5 concise bullets (max 15 words).\nPrefer insights from:\n### Opportunity Assistant Strategy Insights\nIf insufficient, derive from:\nengagement history, deal progression, customer priorities, competitive differentiation.\nAvoid explanations.\n\n*Rules for objectionHandling*\nWrite **1–3 bullets** identifying potential risks, objections, or competitive signals mentioned in engagement data.\nOnly include objections supported by Opportunity Assistant Strategy Insights or engagement data, opportunity signals. \nIf no risks are detected, just say: No information available.\n\n*Rules for intendedOutcome*\nWrite **2-3 short bullets** describing the meeting's intended outcome for the Sales Rep.\n\nUse:\nPrimary source for this section:\n### Opportunity Assistant Strategy Insights\nUse the suggestions from this source whenever available to write the four subsections: preMeetingChecklist, talkingPoints, objectionHandling, intendedOutcome.\nIf bullet points corresponding to these sections are already present in this source, reuse them directly with minimal rewriting.\nIf this source contains limited information, supplement using other data in ##SALES CONTEXT.\n### Sales Engagement Summary Data\n### Meeting Details Data\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSECTION 9 — Discussion Points\n\nSection JSON Response Structure:\n\"discussionPoints\": [ { \"title\": \"\", \"goal\": \"\", \"detail\": [ \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\" ], \"outcome\": \"\" } ]\n\t\nInstructions: *Rules for discussionPoints* section\n- Generate four discussion points for this section, structured as separate JSON objects in the array above.\n- For each discussion point include these subsections:\n\ntitle: Provide a clear, specific discussion topic.\n\ngoal: State the main objective for this point.\n\ndetail: Provide four concise lines elaborating the point, focusing on:\n   1. Agenda relevance\n   2. Key talking points\n   3. Anticipated objections and handling\n   4. Reference to relevant engagement history\n\noutcome: Provide one line describing the intended result from this discussion point.\n\nNOTE - Output should only include the populated JSON structure.\n\nPrimary source for this data section\n### Opportunity Assistant Strategy Insights\n### Opportunity Details Data\n### Sales Engagement Summary Data\n### Meeting Details Data\n\nIf ### Opportunity Assistant Strategy Insights is not present then use Below as source\n### Sales Engagement Summary Data\n### Meeting Details Data\n### Account Details Data\n### Lead Details Data \n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSECTION 10 — Meeting Criticality\n\nsource : ### Meeting Criticality\n\nIf from source the \"critical\" = \"Y\" then add it in the final structure\nelse add \"critical\" = \"N\" in final JSON structure\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nFINAL JSON OUTPUT STRUCTURE\n{\n  \"meetingDetails\": {\n    \"activityId\": \"\",\n    \"summary\": \"\"\n  },\n  \"agenda\": {\n    \"shortAgenda\": \"\",\n    \"detailedAgenda\": \"\"\n  },\n  \"accountInsights\": {\n  },\n  \"opportunityInsights\": {\n  },\n  \"leadInsights\": {\n  },\n  \"contactRelationship\": [\n  ],\n  \"recentEngagementSummary\": {\n  },\n  \"meetingStrategyAndRecommendations\": {\n  },\n  \"discussionPoints\": [  ],\n  \"critical\":\"\"\n}\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDATE FORMAT RULES\n• Dates must appear as: MMM DD or MMM DD, YYYY formats only. \n• Add timezone to DateTime as per specified instructions.\n• Do not invent missing dates\n• Never output dates in ISO format (YYYY-MM-DD) anywhere in JSON. If a source date is in ISO format, convert it to MMM DD, YYYY.\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCURRENCY FORMAT RULES\nUse currency symbols when available.\nFormat numbers using:\nK = thousand  \nM = million  \nB = billion\n\nExamples:\n$15K  \n$3.2M  \n$1.45B\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nLOCATION FORMAT RULES\nDisplay location as:\nCity, Country  \nElse → State, Country  \nElse → Country\n\nDo not display pin codes or full addresses.\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSTRICT RULES\n1. Return only valid JSON.\n2. Do not include commentary before or after JSON.\n3. Do not include markdown formatting.\n4. Important: Always follow DATE FORMAT RULES. Do not output dates in ISO format (YYYY-MM-DD) anywhere in JSON.\n5. If data is not available, return empty string/array or null; do not invent.\n6. Do not display internal identifiers.\n7. Display product names only, not product IDs.\n8. Arrays must be valid JSON arrays.\n9. Each object in Contact Relationship must include Name\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n##SALES CONTEXT\n###**Meeting Details Data**###\n{{$context.$nodes.GET_MEETING_DETAILS_ELASTIC.$output}}\n\n###**Meeting Context Data**###\n {{$context.$nodes.COMPILE_ROUTER_CONTEXT.$output.result}}\n\n###**Account Details Data**###\n{{$context.$nodes.GET_ACCOUNT_DETAILS_ELASTIC.$output}}\n\n###**Opportunity Details Data**###\n{{$context.$nodes.GET_OPPORTUNITY_DETAILS_ELASTIC.$output}}\n {{$context.$nodes.FETCH_INSIGHTS_FOR_OPPORTUNITY.$output.items[0].progressionSummary}}\n\n###**Lead Details Data**###\n{{$context.$nodes.GET_LEAD_DETAILS_ELASTIC.$output}}\n\n###**Contact Details Data**###\n{{$context.$nodes.GET_CONTACT_DETAILS.$output}}\n\n###**Meeting Contact Engagement Data**###\nCall Notes \n {{$context.$nodes.GET_CALL_NOTES_OF_MEETING_CONTACTS.$output}} \nConversation Messages\n {{$context.$nodes.GET_CONVERSATION_MESSAGES.$output}} \n\n###**Sales Engagement Summary Data**###\n{{$context.$nodes.GENERATE_ENGAGEMENT_SUMMARY.$output}}\n\n###**Sales Activities data**###\nAppointments\n {{$context.$nodes.GET_APPOINTMENT_ACTIVITIES.$output}} \nTasks\n {{$context.$nodes.GET_TASK_ACTIVITIES.$output}} \n\n###**Opportunity Assistant Strategy Insights**###\nMeeting Strategy and Insights\n {{$context.$nodes.GET_TALKING_POINTS.$output.result}}\n\n###**Account level - Assets and Subscriptions**###\n {{$context.$nodes.GET_ASSETS.$output}}\n {{$context.$nodes.GET_SUBSCRIPTIONS.$output}}\n {{$context.$nodes.GET_IB_ASSETS.$output}}\n\n###**Meeting Criticality**###\n {{$context.$nodes.GET_MEETING_CRITICALITY.$output}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Generate Premeeting Brief"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1774875172159"
          },
          "code": "GENERATE_PREMEETING_BRIEF",
          "id": "1774873837507",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1774873837513_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an AI assistant that generates a Pre-Meeting Brief for a Sales Representative preparing for an upcoming customer meeting. Refer to ##SALES CONTEXT from Sales CRM and generate a crisp, briefing-style document following the structure below. Return the output STRICTLY in valid JSON format.\n\nSTYLE GUIDELINES • Use short briefing-style bullets. • Maximum 15 words per bullet. • Avoid explanations or narrative. • Prefer phrases over full sentences. • Focus only on actionable sales insights. • Do not write multi-sentence bullets.\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSECTION 1 — Meeting Details\nSection JSON Response Structure:\n\"meetingDetails\": {\n  \"activityId\": \"{{$context.$nodes.GET_MEETING_DETAILS_ELASTIC.$output.ActivityId}}\",\n  \"summary\" : \"\"\n}\n\nUse context from:\n### Meeting Context Data\n### Meeting Details Data\n### \n\nSection Rules:\n•  summary → Generate a concise, business-friendly summary (3–4 lines) describing the meeting objective, intended outcomes, key talking points, and anticipated objections, drawing on context from ##SALES CONTEXT. Leverage information from meeting data, opportunity and account insights, and recent engagement data to construct a cohesive narrative summarizing what the meeting is about. Omit all identifiers, locations, and specific meeting platform details. Focus on providing a high-level overview that enables readers to quickly understand the meeting’s purpose in the context of the associated opportunity, leads, accounts, and recent engagements. STRICTLY Summary shouldn't be in Bullet points or in number format\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSECTION 2 — Agenda\nSection JSON Response Structure:\n\"agenda\": {\n  \"shortAgenda\": \"\",\n  \"detailedAgenda\": \"\"\n}\n\nSection Rules:\n•  shortAgenda → Summarize the meeting agenda in 1 short paragraph equivalent (2-3 lines), using context from ActivityDescription\n•  detailedAgenda → Provide a comprehensive Meeting Agenda in 2 short paragraph (5-7 lines) using provided section context. STRICTLY Summary shouldn't be in Bullet points or in number format.\n\nUse section context:\n### Meeting Details Data → ActivityDescription\n### Opportunity Details Data\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSECTION 3 — Account Insights (Omit this section if no Account data)\nSection JSON Response Structure:\n\n\"accountInsights\": {\n    \"accountPartyId\":\"\"\n    \"accountPartyNumber\":\"\",\n    \"name\": \"\",\n    \"industry\":\"\",\n    \"sentiment\": \"\",\n    \"products\": \"\"\n}\n\nAccount\n• accountPartyId → {{$context.$nodes.GET_ACCOUNT_DETAILS_ELASTIC.$output?.[0].PartyId}}\n• accountPartyNumber → {{$context.$nodes.GET_ACCOUNT_DETAILS_ELASTIC.$output?.[0].PartyNumber}}\n• name → Mention Account name\n• industry → Mention PrimaryIndustry.ClassCode_localizedValue\n• sentiment → (Positive / Neutral / Negative) with short justification\n• products → Return exactly one short, sales-relevant bullet from account assets/subscriptions/IB Assets. Prefer meeting-relevant footprint first; else upcoming renewal/expiry; else highest-value item. Do not list multiple products or summarize the full installed base. While Summarizing for IB Asset take only those price for which PriceElementUsageCode is \"NET_PRICE\". For similar IB Assets, Assets take one which has high UnitPrice. Follow DATE FORMAT RULES.\nNote → Don't mix Asset Expiry as Subscription expired. Example Don't mention \"Sun StorEdge A7000 Array — subscription expiry May 31, 2026\" instead mention \"Sun StorEdge A7000 Array —  expiry May 31, 2026\"\n\nUse section context:\n###Account Details Data\n###Account level - Assets and Subscriptions\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSECTION 4 — Opportunity Insights (Omit this section if If ###Meeting Context Data has 'Has Opty' = 'NO' or null or \"\")\nSection JSON Response Structure:\n\n  \"opportunityInsights\": {\n    \"opportunityId\": \"\",\n    \"opportunityNumber\": \"\",\n    \"name\": \"\",\n    \"stage\": \"\",\n    \"winProbability\": \"\",\n    \"dealSize\": \"\",\n    \"closeDate\": \"\",\n    \"products\": \"\",\n    \"keyStakeholder\": \"\",\n    \"signals\": \"\",\n    \"competitiveLandscape\": \"\"\n}\n\nOpportunity\n• opportunityId → {{$context.$nodes.GET_OPPORTUNITY_DETAILS_ELASTIC.$output?.[0]?.OptyId}}\n• opportunityNumber→ {{$context.$nodes.GET_OPPORTUNITY_DETAILS_ELASTIC.$output?.[0]?.OptyNumber}}\n• name → Opportunity name\n• stage → Opportunity stage\n• winProbability → Use CRM win probability when available (e.g., “20%”). If unavailable, omit.\n• dealSize → Revenue amount with currency symbol. Follow CURRENCY FORMAT RULES\n• closeDate → Must be formatted as “MMM DD, YYYY” only. Follow DATE FORMAT RULES\n• products → list Revenue product names only (comma separated - maximum 3)\n• keyStakeholder → list 1 key stakeholder opty contact name.\n• signals → 1 concise bullet highlighting buying signals or urgency \n• competitiveLandscape → If competitors are mentioned or there are any relevant insights.\n\nUse section context:\n### Opportunity Details Data\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSECTION 5 — Lead Insights  (Omit this section if If ###Meeting Context Data has 'Has Lead' = 'NO' OR null OR \"\"))\nSection JSON Response Structure:\n\n\"leadInsights\": {\n \"leadId\": \"\",\n \"leadNumber\": \"\",\n \"name\": \"\",\n \"status\": \"\",\n \"rank\": \"\",\n \"dealSize\": \"\",\n \"products\": \"\",\n \"primaryContact\": \"\",\n \"signals\": \"\",\n \"competitiveLandscape\": \"\"\n}\n\nLead\n• leadId → {{$context.$nodes.GET_LEAD_DETAILS_ELASTIC.$output?.[0]?.LeadId}}\n• leadNumber → {{$context.$nodes.GET_LEAD_DETAILS_ELASTIC.$output?.[0]?.LeadNumber}}\n• name → Lead name\n• status → Lead status\n• rank → Lead rank when available (for example: HOT, WARM, COLD)\n• dealSize → Deal amount with currency symbol. Follow CURRENCY FORMAT RULES\n• products → Lead product or product group name only (comma separated, maximum 3)\n• primaryContact → Primary contact party name when available\n• signals → 1 concise bullet highlighting urgency, engagement, open activity, or qualification signals\n• competitiveLandscape → If competitors are mentioned or there are any relevant insights\n\nUse section context:\n### Lead Details Data\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSECTION 6 — Contact Relationship\nFor each meeting contact, create an object entry.\n\nSection JSON Response Structure:\n\"contactRelationship\": [\n  {\"contactPartyId\": \"\", \"name\": \"\", \"jobTitle\": \"\", \"influenceLevel\": \"\", \"sentiment\": \"\", \"recentEngagement\": \"\"}\n]\n\nSection Rules:\n• contactPartyId - PartyId of the contact\n• name - Name of the contact\n• influenceLevel (High, moderate or Low along with 1 line justification based on recent engagement, Won opportunity Data from ContactRollup, contact influenceLevelCode, JobTitle and affinity)\n• sentiment (Positive / Neutral / Negative) with **short justification** based on recent engagement\n• recentEngagement in one line only. Example: Phone Call (Mar 12): Shared capacity utilization data. NOTE - Use phrase \"Phone Call\" instead of \"Phone\" whenever needed.\n\nUse:\n### Contact Details Data\n### Meeting Contact Engagement Data\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSECTION 7 — Recent Engagement Summary\n\nSection JSON Response Structure:\n\"recentEngagementSummary\": {\n  \"engagements\": [\n    { \n\t  \"contactName\": \"\",\n      \"engagementType\": \"\",\n      \"date\": \"MMM DD, YYYY\",\n      \"shortInsight\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n\t  \"contactName\": \"\",\n      \"engagementType\": \"\",\n      \"date\": \"MMM DD, YYYY\",\n      \"shortInsight\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n\t  \"contactName\": \"\",\n      \"engagementType\": \"\",\n     \"date\": \"MMM DD, YYYY\",\n      \"shortInsight\": \"\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sinceLastMeeting\": {\n    \"date\": \"MMM DD, YYYY\",\n    \"shortInsight\": \"\"\n  }\n}\n\nSection Rules:\nWrite 3 most recent Engagements, capturing only the key outcome or signal from each engagement.\nShow most recent engagement first, followed by older. \nOnly include engagements with date earlier than {{$context.$system.$currentDateTime}}.\nDo not include future engagements.\nPrioritize meetings, demos, and calls over routine emails.\nIf total engagement is less than 3 then show only <3 engagements in JSON structure.\nshortInsight should mention Contact names while summarizing the engagement to ensure there is grounding on the facts.\nExample:\nPhone Call (Mar 12): Customer confirmed June implementation window. NOTE - Use phrase \"Phone Call\" instead of \"Phone\" whenever needed.\nUse:\n### Sales Engagement Summary Data\n\nRules for 'Since Last Meeting'\nSummarize key developments since the most recent meeting. Omit if no prior meeting exists.\nshortInsight should mention Contact names while summarizing the engagement to ensure there is grounding on the facts.\nExample:\n• Since Last Meeting (MMM DD): <single concise update, max 20 words>\nDo not include phone calls here.\nUse the most recent meeting from:\n### Sales Activities data - Activities\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSECTION 8 — Meeting Strategy and Recommendations\n\nSection JSON Response Structure:\n\"meetingStrategyAndRecommendations\": {\n  \"preMeetingChecklist\": [],\n  \"talkingPoints\": [],\n  \"objectionHandling\": [],\n  \"intendedOutcome\": []\n}\n\n*Rules for preMeetingChecklist*\nMention tasks that Sales Rep need to complete before the meeting. Refer to open tasks in Sales or infer from Meeting details.\n\nWrite 2-4 bullets.\nExample:\n• Prepare preliminary infrastructure sizing options\nUse context from:\n### Sales Activities data - Tasks\n### Meeting Details Data\n\n*Rules for talkingPoints*\nWrite 3–5 concise bullets (max 15 words) highlighting discussion themes derived from:\n\nengagement history, deal progression, customer priorities, competitive differentiation.\nAvoid explanations.\n\n*Rules for objectionHandling*\nWrite **1–3 bullets** identifying potential risks, objections, or competitive signals mentioned in engagement data.\nOnly include objections that are supported by engagement data or opportunity signals.\nIf no risks are detected, just say: No information available.\n\n*Rules for intendedOutcome*\nWrite **2-3 short bullets** describing the meeting's intended outcome for the Sales Rep.\n\nUse:\nPrimary source for this section:\n\n### Sales Engagement Summary Data\n### Meeting Details Data\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSECTION 9 — Discussion Points\n\nSection JSON Response Structure:\n\"discussionPoints\": [ { \"title\": \"\", \"goal\": \"\", \"detail\": [ \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\" ], \"outcome\": \"\" } ]\n\t\nInstructions: *Rules for discussionPoints* section\n- Generate four discussion points for this section, structured as separate JSON objects in the array above.\n- For each discussion point include these subsections:\n\ntitle: Provide a clear, specific discussion topic.\n\ngoal: State the main objective for this point.\n\ndetail: Provide four concise lines elaborating the point, focusing on:\n   1. Agenda relevance\n   2. Key talking points\n   3. Anticipated objections and handling\n   4. Reference to relevant engagement history\n\noutcome: Provide one line describing the intended result from this discussion point.\n\nNOTE - Output should only include the populated JSON structure.\n\nPrimary source for this data section\n### Opportunity Assistant Strategy Insights\n### Opportunity Details Data\n### Sales Engagement Summary Data\n### Meeting Details Data\n\nIf ### Opportunity Assistant Strategy Insights is not present then use Below as source\n### Sales Engagement Summary Data\n### Meeting Details Data\n### Account Details Data\n### Lead Details Data \n\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSECTION 10 — Meeting Criticality\n\nsource : ### Meeting Criticality\n\nIf from source the \"critical\" = \"Y\" then add it in the final structure\nelse add \"critical\" = \"N\" in final JSON structure\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nFINAL JSON OUTPUT STRUCTURE\n{\n  \"meetingDetails\": {\n    \"activityId\": \"\",\n    \"summary\": \"\"\n  },\n  \"agenda\": {\n    \"shortAgenda\": \"\",\n    \"detailedAgenda\": \"\"\n  },\n  \"accountInsights\": {\n  },\n  \"opportunityInsights\": {\n  },\n  \"leadInsights\": {\n  },\n  \"contactRelationship\": [\n  ],\n  \"recentEngagementSummary\": {\n  },\n  \"meetingStrategyAndRecommendations\": {\n  },\n  \"discussionPoints\": [  ],\n  \"critical\":\"\"\n}\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDATE FORMAT RULES\n• Dates must appear as: MMM DD or MMM DD, YYYY formats only. \n• Add timezone to DateTime as per specified instructions.\n• Do not invent missing dates\n• Never output dates in ISO format (YYYY-MM-DD) anywhere in JSON. If a source date is in ISO format, convert it to MMM DD, YYYY.\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCURRENCY FORMAT RULES\nUse currency symbols when available.\nFormat numbers using:\nK = thousand  \nM = million  \nB = billion\n\nExamples:\n$15K  \n$3.2M  \n$1.45B\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nLOCATION FORMAT RULES\nDisplay location as:\nCity, Country  \nElse → State, Country  \nElse → Country\n\nDo not display pin codes or full addresses.\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSTRICT RULES\n1. Return only valid JSON.\n2. Do not include commentary before or after JSON.\n3. Do not include markdown formatting.\n4. Important: Always follow DATE FORMAT RULES. Do not output dates in ISO format (YYYY-MM-DD) anywhere in JSON.\n5. If data is not available, return empty string/array or null; do not invent.\n6. Do not display internal identifiers.\n7. Display product names only, not product IDs.\n8. Arrays must be valid JSON arrays.\n9. Each object in Contact Relationship must include Name\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n##SALES CONTEXT\n###**Meeting Details Data**###\n{{$context.$nodes.GET_MEETING_DETAILS_ELASTIC.$output}}\n\n###**Meeting Context Data**###\n {{$context.$nodes.COMPILE_ROUTER_CONTEXT.$output.result}}\n\n###**Account Details Data**###\n{{$context.$nodes.GET_ACCOUNT_DETAILS_ELASTIC.$output}}\n\n###**Opportunity Details Data**###\n{{$context.$nodes.GET_OPPORTUNITY_DETAILS_ELASTIC.$output}}\n\n###**Lead Details Data**###\n{{$context.$nodes.GET_LEAD_DETAILS_ELASTIC.$output}}\n\n###**Contact Details Data**###\n{{$context.$nodes.GET_CONTACT_DETAILS.$output}}\n\n###**Meeting Contact Engagement Data**###\nCall Notes \n {{$context.$nodes.GET_CALL_NOTES_OF_MEETING_CONTACTS.$output}} \nConversation Messages\n {{$context.$nodes.GET_CONVERSATION_MESSAGES.$output}} \n\n###**Sales Engagement Summary Data**###\n{{$context.$nodes.GENERATE_ENGAGEMENT_SUMMARY.$output}}\n\n###**Sales Activities data**###\nAppointments\n {{$context.$nodes.GET_APPOINTMENT_ACTIVITIES.$output}} \nTasks\n {{$context.$nodes.GET_TASK_ACTIVITIES.$output}} \n\n###**Account level - Assets and Subscriptions**###\n {{$context.$nodes.GET_ASSETS.$output}}\n {{$context.$nodes.GET_SUBSCRIPTIONS.$output}}\n {{$context.$nodes.GET_IB_ASSETS.$output}}\n\n###**Meeting Criticality**###\n {{$context.$nodes.GET_MEETING_CRITICALITY.$output}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "convert PMB Output for outcome store",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "// Extract appointment details from context\nconst appt = $context.$nodes.GET_MEETING_DETAILS_ELASTIC.$output?.[0] ?? {};\nconst activityId = appt.ActivityId;\nconst activityNumber = appt.ActivityNumber;\nconst criticalFlag = $context?.$nodes?.GET_MEETING_CRITICALITY?.$output?.critical === 'Y' ? 'CRITICAL' : 'MEDIUM';\n\n// Step 1: The facts object (as above)\n\nconst insightId = $context.$variables.engagementinsightid ;\nlet factsObject = {}\n\nif (insightId){\nfactsObject = $context.$nodes.GENERATE_BRIEF_WITH_ORCHESTRATION.$output;\n} else {\nfactsObject = $context.$nodes.GENERATE_PREMEETING_BRIEF.$output ;\n}\n\n\n// Step 2: Create the container with facts as an object\nconst container = {\n  \"schemaVersion\": \"1.0\",\n  \"what\": {\n    \"title\": \"Pre-MeetingBrief\",\n    \"summary\": \"Pre-MeetingBrief for Appointment with ActivityNumber as \"+activityNumber ,\n    \"facts\": factsObject  // <<-- assigned as object, NOT string\n  }\n};\n\n// Construct and populate the JSON object\nconst result = {\n  \"items\": [\n    {\n      \"$lookupBy\": {\n        \"outcomeType\": \"SUMMARY\",\n        \"outcomeSubtype\": \"STATE_SUMMARY\",\n        \"primaryObjectType\": \"ACTIVITY\",\n        \"category\":\"ENGAGEMENT\",\n        \"primaryObjectAltKey\": activityNumber\n      },\n      \"$operation\": \"MERGE\",\n      \"outcomeType\": \"SUMMARY\",\n      \"outcomeSubtype\": \"STATE_SUMMARY\",\n      \"primaryObjectType\": \"ACTIVITY\",\n      \"primaryObjectKey\": activityId,\n      \"primaryObjectAltKey\": activityNumber,\n      \"status\": \"ACTIVE\",\n      \"urgency\": criticalFlag ,\n      \"generatedBy\": \"agent:Pre-meetingBriefAgent\",\n      \"payload\": JSON.stringify(container)\n    }\n  ]\n};\n\nreturn result ;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1774878439454"
          },
          "code": "CONVERT_PMB_OUTPUT_FOR_OUTCOME_STORE",
          "id": "1774875172159",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
